WEBVTT

00:07.007 --> 00:09.009
[ominous music]

00:11.469 --> 00:13.763
[fire crackling]

00:13.847 --> 00:16.141
[people murmuring]

00:16.224 --> 00:18.017
[man panting]

00:18.101 --> 00:20.186
[man] There's a fire
at the back of the building!

00:20.270 --> 00:22.522
[crowd clamoring]

00:25.233 --> 00:29.195
We have to find whoever murdered Momoka
and burn them in the Fire of Judgement.

00:29.279 --> 00:31.573
A witch hunt game, huh?
This ought to be good.

00:33.992 --> 00:35.326
[Usagi] The game started.

00:36.911 --> 00:38.121
Rain check on our date?

00:40.123 --> 00:42.584
All right, let's go witch hunting!

00:42.667 --> 00:46.004
[overlapping chatter]

00:57.474 --> 00:59.184
You, you're always with her.

01:00.060 --> 01:01.478
Why weren't you with her today?

01:02.103 --> 01:03.354
[Asahi] What?

01:03.438 --> 01:06.566
That's true, you weren't.
What happened? You fight?

01:06.649 --> 01:07.484
[gun cocks]

01:07.567 --> 01:09.444
- Are you our witch?
- It's not me!

01:09.527 --> 01:11.404
I guess we'll know
when we throw you in the fire!

01:11.488 --> 01:13.073
I was in my room! She was my friend!

01:13.156 --> 01:16.034
So you're with her everyday,
except the day she gets killed.

01:16.910 --> 01:17.744
[snickers]

01:17.827 --> 01:21.331
Great, then we're agreed,
she's the witch. Take her to the fire!

01:21.414 --> 01:23.958
- [crowd clamoring]
- Come on, let's go!

01:24.584 --> 01:26.002
- [Asahi] Let me go!
- Come on!

01:26.086 --> 01:27.796
I didn't kill her!

01:28.379 --> 01:31.132
- Let me go!
- That's enough!

01:31.758 --> 01:33.384
Put down Asahi.

01:34.052 --> 01:35.762
We're all suspects in this game.

01:36.763 --> 01:38.515
[panting]

01:39.140 --> 01:42.727
Where were all of you?
And what were… were you all doing?

01:43.311 --> 01:44.813
And can you prove it?

01:47.232 --> 01:51.277
I can prove that you and I were having
a good time in bed.

01:52.487 --> 01:56.407
Everyone will take turns explaining
what you did in the past hour.

01:56.491 --> 01:58.159
[gasps]
Look, blood!

02:01.955 --> 02:04.457
- I can explain this.
- Finally, this is getting interesting.

02:04.541 --> 02:06.751
- I say she's the witch!
- You're wrong.

02:06.835 --> 02:08.753
This is Hatter's blood.

02:08.837 --> 02:10.713
[crowd murmuring]

02:11.422 --> 02:15.218
I was examining Hatter's body.
That's how the blood got on me.

02:15.301 --> 02:16.344
His body?

02:19.347 --> 02:21.057
Hatter was murdered.

02:22.475 --> 02:25.478
- [Uda] Hatter was killed?
- [Mizuki] Why didn't you tell us?

02:26.062 --> 02:28.815
The executives believed
that this might throw everyone

02:28.898 --> 02:30.066
into a panic.

02:30.150 --> 02:33.528
What else are you… you people hiding
from us? Huh? What?

02:33.611 --> 02:36.322
- [Tamotsu] No more secrets, okay?
- Calm down.

02:40.118 --> 02:42.495
I took this bullet from Hatter's body.

02:43.121 --> 02:46.499
Its caliber is the same
as those we have here at the Beach.

02:46.583 --> 02:47.625
Uh-huh?

02:48.209 --> 02:52.881
This means that someone here
at the Beach killed Hatter.

02:52.964 --> 02:54.924
[crows murmurs]

02:56.718 --> 02:57.552
[gasps]

02:58.261 --> 03:01.347
Do you think that maybe
the witch killed Hatter?

03:03.308 --> 03:06.394
I mean, that doesn't sound so crazy,
am I right?

03:06.477 --> 03:08.605
Uh, the witch could be one of them--

03:10.648 --> 03:12.358
- [blade slashes]
- [thuds]

03:12.442 --> 03:14.068
[crowd exclaiming]

03:14.152 --> 03:15.987
I found her annoying.

03:16.070 --> 03:18.239
Let's just burn everyone.

03:19.532 --> 03:21.326
[breathes shakily]

03:22.827 --> 03:25.413
[Aguni] If someone here is the witch,

03:26.831 --> 03:29.792
then everyone in this room except me
could be the witch.

03:32.837 --> 03:35.882
So, who here is the witch? Step forward.

03:42.430 --> 03:44.224
If no one here will admit it,

03:44.933 --> 03:46.893
then all of you will burn.

03:46.976 --> 03:48.603
[crowd murmuring]

03:49.938 --> 03:51.064
Yahoo!

03:51.147 --> 03:53.608
- [gunshots]
- [crowd screaming]

03:55.443 --> 03:57.654
[crowd clamoring in panic]

04:01.032 --> 04:02.325
- [Niragi] Woo-hoo!
- [gunshots]

04:02.408 --> 04:03.618
Get up!

04:06.871 --> 04:08.248
1 PER PERSON

04:09.290 --> 04:10.291
[Usagi] Come on!

04:12.126 --> 04:14.504
Comb through all of them, got that?

04:14.587 --> 04:15.922
No one escapes!

04:16.005 --> 04:17.423
[Yu] Are you really gonna do what he says?

04:17.507 --> 04:19.467
We worked together as a team until today.

04:19.550 --> 04:21.135
- [Niragi] Eh?
- If the game doesn't end

04:21.219 --> 04:22.095
after you do this,

04:22.178 --> 04:24.097
- then eventually, we'll have to kill--
- [gunshots]

04:24.180 --> 04:25.515
Woo-hoo!

04:26.182 --> 04:29.018
Burn him. He's of no use to us now.

04:29.852 --> 04:31.229
[Niragi] Let's go, guys!

04:31.312 --> 04:33.314
[suspenseful music]

04:37.068 --> 04:39.862
[muffled grunt]

04:39.946 --> 04:41.948
[grunting continues]

04:49.539 --> 04:51.541
[theme music]

05:47.305 --> 05:49.432
[people screaming]

05:49.515 --> 05:50.808
[man] Suzuka, hurry!

05:53.144 --> 05:54.937
[screaming]

05:58.357 --> 05:59.984
[breathing nervously]

06:03.279 --> 06:04.781
- [gunshots]
- [people grunting]

06:05.531 --> 06:09.077
We have others to question
and time's running out.

06:10.703 --> 06:13.456
- [gunshots]
- [crowd screaming]

06:15.666 --> 06:17.710
[panting]

06:23.049 --> 06:24.550
Listen, hide inside this room.

06:24.634 --> 06:26.636
Alone? I want to stay with you.

06:26.719 --> 06:28.721
I have to go and find someone.

06:29.347 --> 06:30.765
Let me come too, Usagi.

06:30.848 --> 06:33.101
It's sure to be game over for me
if I stay here.

06:35.228 --> 06:37.063
[pants]
It's me, Tatta!

06:39.524 --> 06:41.192
Listen, hear me out.

06:41.275 --> 06:43.861
I think we should work together
like we have before.

06:48.241 --> 06:49.784
Help me find Arisu.

06:50.952 --> 06:52.120
[gunshots in distance]

06:52.954 --> 06:53.788
[people screaming]

06:53.871 --> 06:55.540
We gotta keep moving,
they're getting close.

06:55.623 --> 06:56.791
They're getting closer.

06:56.874 --> 06:58.084
Come on, hurry.

07:00.044 --> 07:02.672
[people screaming]

07:03.339 --> 07:04.841
[Suzuka yelps]

07:04.924 --> 07:06.259
Suzuka!

07:08.970 --> 07:11.889
Don't shoot, she's not the witch! I swear!

07:12.473 --> 07:13.933
- [gunshots]
- [shrieks]

07:16.060 --> 07:17.603
Don't think, just shoot.

07:19.188 --> 07:20.857
[sobbing]
Please…

07:21.357 --> 07:23.818
[Suzuka whimpers]
Don't kill me.

07:24.986 --> 07:26.404
It's not me.

07:27.530 --> 07:29.115
- Please!
- [breathes shakily]

07:29.198 --> 07:30.908
Don't do it!

07:30.992 --> 07:32.326
I have to

07:32.410 --> 07:33.369
or I'm next.

07:33.453 --> 07:35.371
- [sobs]
- You're not human!

07:35.455 --> 07:36.456
[gunshots]

07:36.539 --> 07:38.541
[slow eerie music]

07:58.060 --> 07:59.979
[fire crackling]

08:18.998 --> 08:21.250
[slow eerie music continues]

08:42.438 --> 08:44.524
[Kuina] They've all gone crazy.

08:47.193 --> 08:48.861
Not their smartest move.

08:49.737 --> 08:51.739
Why would they go so far just to survive?

08:52.323 --> 08:56.244
There's no way to find out
who the witch is this way.

09:00.039 --> 09:02.833
You could be the witch. Right, Kuina?

09:05.878 --> 09:07.171
Or it could be you.

09:13.844 --> 09:14.720
[scoffs]

09:31.529 --> 09:33.531
[foreboding music]

09:35.449 --> 09:37.868
- [people screaming]
- [gunshots]

09:37.952 --> 09:40.329
- [gunshots]
- [thuds]

09:43.666 --> 09:45.376
Herd them out through the courtyard.

09:45.960 --> 09:48.546
It'll be easier to move their bodies.
[chuckles]

09:50.047 --> 09:52.717
[Niragi on radio]
Some of them are hiding inside the hotel.

09:54.510 --> 09:56.053
[Last Boss] But I'll force them all out.

09:57.013 --> 09:58.180
[thuds]

09:58.264 --> 10:00.433
[liquid sloshing]

10:00.516 --> 10:01.601
[lighter clicks]

10:04.478 --> 10:07.732
- [lighter clanks]
- [fire roars]

10:14.697 --> 10:15.906
[Usagi] Arisu!

10:18.409 --> 10:20.202
- [Usagi] Arisu!
- [Tatta] Arisu.

10:21.912 --> 10:22.872
[Usagi] Arisu!

10:22.955 --> 10:24.498
[Tatta] Arisu!

10:24.582 --> 10:25.916
[all panting]

10:26.000 --> 10:27.376
[Asahi] Arisu!

10:29.879 --> 10:31.422
- [Asahi] Arisu!
- [Usagi] Arisu!

10:32.048 --> 10:36.260
GASOLINE, KEROSENE

10:36.344 --> 10:38.971
- [fire roaring]
- [fire alarm ringing]

10:39.055 --> 10:41.057
[tense music]

10:45.186 --> 10:47.188
[pants]

10:56.113 --> 10:57.031
[Asahi shrieks]

10:58.866 --> 11:01.744
- [Usagi] Asahi?
- [breathing heavily]

11:05.331 --> 11:08.918
[mumbling shakily]

11:11.879 --> 11:13.255
Are you okay?

11:15.466 --> 11:16.926
I… I can't do this.

11:25.810 --> 11:27.311
Have you seen Arisu?

11:30.523 --> 11:32.358
He's in the main building.

11:32.441 --> 11:34.443
[ominous music]

11:36.987 --> 11:38.614
- [Tatta] Arisu!
- [Joe] Arisu!

11:42.952 --> 11:44.578
[man] Come here you bastard!

11:45.579 --> 11:47.748
- [grunts]
- [yells]

11:47.832 --> 11:49.792
[grunting]

11:53.546 --> 11:54.964
- [gunshot]
- [Joe grunts]

11:58.175 --> 12:00.344
Joe.
[breathing heavily]

12:01.303 --> 12:04.140
- Saiko, you bitch!
- [gunshot]

12:04.223 --> 12:05.891
[both groan]

12:06.434 --> 12:09.061
- [Saiko grunts]
- [panting]

12:10.104 --> 12:11.313
Where is Arisu?

12:13.441 --> 12:14.650
[Saiko] He's somewhere on…

12:16.569 --> 12:17.736
the fourth floor.

12:18.404 --> 12:20.072
How do you know that?

12:20.698 --> 12:22.616
I saw Niragi come out of a room there.

12:23.993 --> 12:25.202
[grunts]

12:26.370 --> 12:27.288
[gasps]

12:28.706 --> 12:31.083
[fire alarm ringing]

12:33.544 --> 12:34.879
[door opens]

12:37.339 --> 12:38.424
[door closes]

12:50.352 --> 12:52.021
- [Ann] What do you want?
- Hey.

12:52.855 --> 12:54.398
What are you doing?

12:54.482 --> 12:56.192
[Ann] Come here and give me a hand.

12:56.942 --> 12:59.570
Are you the witch?

13:00.196 --> 13:01.739
[Ann] Unfortunately, not.

13:03.324 --> 13:04.366
What about you?

13:06.994 --> 13:08.078
I'm guessing not.

13:10.206 --> 13:13.834
Anyone trying to find the witch
on their own is not one.

13:13.918 --> 13:16.962
If you were the witch,
you'd be hiding right now

13:17.046 --> 13:18.839
or having fun killing people.

13:19.757 --> 13:21.759
Again, what are you doing?

13:22.801 --> 13:24.303
Looking for the witch.

13:26.430 --> 13:28.057
[Ann] Ah, here it is.

13:28.641 --> 13:29.934
[Kuina] What's that?

13:30.017 --> 13:32.353
Cyanoacrylate glue.

13:32.937 --> 13:34.313
[Ann] It's a super glue.

13:34.897 --> 13:35.940
[Kuina] And?

13:36.774 --> 13:40.402
And if we heat this up
and apply it on the murder weapon,

13:40.486 --> 13:43.197
all the moisture
in the cyanoacrylate will evaporate

13:43.280 --> 13:45.241
and hopefully, leave behind fingerprints.

13:45.908 --> 13:47.076
Fingerprints?

13:49.078 --> 13:50.829
Then I'll be able to use cocoa powder

13:50.913 --> 13:54.041
to dust for fingerprints
on the knife handle.

13:54.124 --> 13:56.377
After I lift the fingerprints
with cellophane tape,

13:56.460 --> 13:57.962
I'll be able to identify the witch.

14:00.589 --> 14:02.174
What did you do before you came here?

14:02.258 --> 14:04.343
Forensics, Tokyo Metro Police.

14:05.511 --> 14:08.639
Pretty good.
We can clear the game with this.

14:13.060 --> 14:15.062
[ominous music]

14:19.024 --> 14:21.068
You, go ahead.

14:21.819 --> 14:22.861
What?

14:24.029 --> 14:26.949
We need you to help us to clear this game.

14:32.496 --> 14:34.957
- [fire alarm ringing]
- [man 1] Run, come on!

14:35.040 --> 14:37.710
[people screaming frantically]

14:41.547 --> 14:42.965
[man 2] Down there!

14:46.135 --> 14:48.637
[screaming continues]

14:53.267 --> 14:56.186
[muffled grunt]

14:56.270 --> 14:58.272
[dramatic music]

15:09.491 --> 15:10.951
[thuds]

15:11.035 --> 15:13.162
[muffled cough]

15:18.125 --> 15:20.628
- [fire alarm ringing]
- [people screaming]

15:21.629 --> 15:22.880
Run for the annex!

15:26.383 --> 15:28.510
- [gunshots]
- [panicked gasp]

15:29.720 --> 15:31.347
[gunshots]

15:33.015 --> 15:35.476
[gasping]

15:37.019 --> 15:39.104
- [screaming]
- [gunshots]

15:45.319 --> 15:47.071
- [gunshot]
- [woman screams]

15:47.154 --> 15:48.489
[man] No!

15:48.572 --> 15:50.574
[sad emotional music]

15:57.081 --> 15:58.874
[boy 1] Okay, aim!

15:58.958 --> 16:00.960
- [boy 1 laughing]
- [boy 2] Let's do this, come on!

16:01.043 --> 16:04.129
- [boy 1] Steady, aim…
- [laughing continues]

16:05.047 --> 16:06.006
[yelps]

16:06.090 --> 16:07.925
- [laughter]
- Did you see that?

16:08.008 --> 16:12.471
Hey! Stand up!
We're not done with you yet! Come on!

16:12.554 --> 16:14.431
- [boy 2] Get up!
- [Niragi whimpers]

16:14.515 --> 16:16.642
If you don't move, you can have lunch.

16:17.559 --> 16:21.772
- Pissy rice soup!
- [boys laughing]

16:21.855 --> 16:23.857
- [boy 3] Okay, whose turn is it?
- [boy 4] Mine! Mine!

16:23.941 --> 16:26.652
- [boy 3] Come on, stand up! Come on!
- [breathing nervously]

16:27.486 --> 16:29.571
[boy 3] On your feet, Niragi!

16:30.656 --> 16:32.825
[people screaming]

16:35.285 --> 16:39.206
[Chishiya] Don't you get tired
of bullying people weaker than you?

16:41.834 --> 16:43.669
And where were you hiding?

16:44.753 --> 16:47.047
Oh, there are lots of places
for me to hide.

16:48.465 --> 16:50.884
You really get on my nerves,
you know that?

16:50.968 --> 16:53.053
Think you're so goddamn smart.

16:53.637 --> 16:55.556
[Niragi]
Acting like you're so damn clever!

16:56.223 --> 16:57.224
[scoffs]

16:57.307 --> 16:59.184
I don't have to act clever.

17:00.644 --> 17:01.603
[snorts]

17:03.272 --> 17:05.357
- [clicking]
- Okay then.

17:10.029 --> 17:11.989
Why don't we put an end to this right now?

17:15.784 --> 17:17.619
- [fire alarm ringing]
- [clatters]

17:26.253 --> 17:28.547
- [grunts]
- [sword swooshing]

17:28.630 --> 17:30.716
[breathing heavily]

17:31.300 --> 17:32.217
[both grunt]

17:36.555 --> 17:38.807
[Last Boss snickers]

17:42.352 --> 17:43.937
[both grunting]

17:54.490 --> 17:56.492
[light suspenseful music]

18:22.768 --> 18:24.686
[both grunting]

18:34.154 --> 18:36.073
[Kuina groans]

18:40.244 --> 18:42.246
- [grunts]
- [clattering]

18:45.415 --> 18:46.834
[clanking]

18:51.505 --> 18:53.132
[electricity crackling]

18:57.010 --> 18:58.470
- [grunts]
- [Kuina groans]

18:58.554 --> 18:59.930
- [thuds]
- [clattering]

19:00.013 --> 19:02.015
[upbeat techno music playing]

19:04.726 --> 19:07.062
[Last Boss cackling]

19:08.438 --> 19:11.108
Whoa, pretty good.

19:11.191 --> 19:13.068
What'd you do before you got here?

19:14.486 --> 19:16.280
I sold wedding gowns.

19:37.384 --> 19:40.429
[Kuina's father yells, grunts]

19:42.806 --> 19:45.225
- [shouts]
- [grunts]

19:45.309 --> 19:46.852
[shouting]

19:47.769 --> 19:49.396
[panting]

19:51.315 --> 19:54.568
[exhales loudly]

19:57.321 --> 19:59.114
[yells]

19:59.198 --> 20:00.824
[grunts]

20:02.951 --> 20:04.453
- [shouts]
- [grunts]

20:04.953 --> 20:06.747
[gasps for breath]

20:06.830 --> 20:08.707
Never hesitate to strike.

20:12.461 --> 20:15.297
[coughing]

20:18.800 --> 20:20.802
[soft music]

20:46.036 --> 20:47.412
[soft chuckle]

20:49.456 --> 20:50.457
[clattering]

20:50.540 --> 20:52.793
Not in my house!

20:52.876 --> 20:54.002
- [slaps]
- [grunts]

20:55.087 --> 20:58.423
[Kuina's father]
You're a boy! A boy, not a girl!

20:58.507 --> 21:02.302
[Kuina's father growls angrily]

21:02.386 --> 21:04.388
[sentimental music]

21:08.558 --> 21:09.518
[Kuina's father] Hikari.

21:11.144 --> 21:12.479
Don't ever come back.

21:31.123 --> 21:33.375
Hikari? Hikari?

21:42.843 --> 21:45.637
[exhales deeply]

21:53.812 --> 21:55.063
[Kuina] But enough about me.

21:58.775 --> 22:00.068
What about you?

22:05.282 --> 22:08.910
[Chishiya] Our main power supply's
been diverted since this game started.

22:08.994 --> 22:10.162
[Niragi] What?

22:10.245 --> 22:13.165
The electricity we've always used
from these power generators…

22:13.248 --> 22:15.500
was switched to the hotel's power supply.

22:16.043 --> 22:19.421
That means that whoever's running the game

22:19.504 --> 22:21.006
snuck into the Beach

22:21.715 --> 22:23.425
and controls its power from underground.

22:24.968 --> 22:26.470
What the hell are you saying?

22:27.054 --> 22:29.514
[Chishiya] I think you know
who the witch is. That it's…

22:29.598 --> 22:31.058
someone close to you.

22:31.683 --> 22:33.560
[Niragi]
You saying you think I'm the witch?

22:33.643 --> 22:35.353
Sorry, but you're wrong.

22:36.271 --> 22:38.607
[Chishiya] Only the executive members
have information

22:38.690 --> 22:40.859
on how the power grid operates.

22:40.942 --> 22:45.947
I also know that only the executives have
the key to access the underground.

22:47.532 --> 22:50.827
And I'll kill all the executives
to get that key, starting with you.

22:52.746 --> 22:55.582
Sorry, but I can't let you do that.
I've got plans.

22:55.665 --> 22:56.708
Uh-huh.

22:58.919 --> 23:00.003
Back off!

23:04.341 --> 23:06.968
- What the hell was that?
- [gunshot]

23:11.098 --> 23:13.225
[fire roars]

23:13.308 --> 23:16.686
[Niragi screaming]

23:22.234 --> 23:23.944
[screaming continues]

23:27.197 --> 23:29.616
[keyboard clacking]

23:29.699 --> 23:31.243
[Last Boss] Robert Edwin Peary.

23:31.326 --> 23:34.913
An explorer who devoted his entire life
to reaching the North Pole.

23:34.996 --> 23:36.123
THE BOUND UNIVERSE

23:36.206 --> 23:38.083
He failed to reach it several times.

23:38.166 --> 23:42.045
In fact, he lost eight of his toes
on one particular expedition.

23:42.129 --> 23:44.631
However, in 1909, he became

23:44.714 --> 23:47.300
the first Westerner
to reach the North Pole.

23:47.384 --> 23:49.177
[knocking on door]

23:49.261 --> 23:51.346
[typing pauses]

23:51.429 --> 23:53.390
[Last Boss' mother]
I'm leaving your dinner here.

23:54.933 --> 23:57.060
[typing resumes]

24:00.063 --> 24:03.233
[Last Boss] As he marched ever forward
towards certain death,

24:03.316 --> 24:06.194
people often wondered
what drove him to do so.

24:06.987 --> 24:10.198
I believe,
that by facing the possibility of death,

24:10.282 --> 24:13.827
it was in fact,
his way to feel truly alive.

24:13.910 --> 24:16.496
When will I, too, feel truly alive?

24:16.580 --> 24:17.622
[Last Boss' mother] Hey.

24:17.706 --> 24:19.624
[typing pauses]

24:19.708 --> 24:22.586
What can… Mom do?

24:27.299 --> 24:28.842
[typing resumes]

24:31.678 --> 24:33.346
[Last Boss] Even though I am alive,

24:33.430 --> 24:37.309
I am in a place where I cannot even choose
what it is that I eat.

24:37.893 --> 24:40.979
I lived this life
without having any consciousness of death.

24:41.563 --> 24:44.399
How should I feel, then,
about truly living life?

24:47.110 --> 24:50.739
I need to escape
from this temporary home I live in.

24:51.823 --> 24:55.160
I want to live in the real world.

25:08.423 --> 25:09.549
And then…

25:10.217 --> 25:12.344
I came to this land.

25:18.642 --> 25:21.186
[flies buzzing]

25:23.355 --> 25:26.149
[running footsteps]

25:26.233 --> 25:29.194
[panting]

25:29.277 --> 25:30.612
[phone chiming]

25:30.695 --> 25:34.241
[announcer] Game cleared. Congratulations.

25:34.324 --> 25:37.744
GAME CLEARED
CONGRATULATIONS

25:38.578 --> 25:42.374
- [phone clatters]
- [groans]

25:43.959 --> 25:45.961
[Last Boss]
This was the first time I felt it.

25:46.836 --> 25:48.505
The joy of life.

25:52.592 --> 25:54.594
[soft emotional music]

25:58.056 --> 26:00.350
[scissors snipping]

26:17.325 --> 26:19.327
[soft emotional music continues]

26:41.016 --> 26:42.309
I have heard…

26:43.059 --> 26:45.770
I heard you were a tattooist
in the old world.

26:48.315 --> 26:49.190
Yeah.

26:52.110 --> 26:54.571
I want you to tattoo
something astounding on my body.

26:56.948 --> 27:01.202
So astounding that it won't be acceptable
in the old world.

27:09.461 --> 27:11.796
[Last Boss]
By doing this, I pledged to myself

27:12.839 --> 27:16.426
that I will live in this world forever.

27:21.681 --> 27:23.683
[upbeat techno music playing faintly]

27:25.727 --> 27:26.728
My story…

27:27.604 --> 27:30.732
[snickers]
…has no past.

27:32.692 --> 27:36.446
[Kuina laughing]

27:40.116 --> 27:41.493
[laughing continues]

27:43.078 --> 27:44.662
Oh, sorry, sorry.

27:45.372 --> 27:46.998
I understand it all now.

27:48.708 --> 27:51.544
I always thought
that you and I were the very same.

27:52.712 --> 27:53.880
Me and you?

27:57.884 --> 28:00.053
Both of us hate our past.

28:01.763 --> 28:02.722
[chuckles]

28:04.516 --> 28:07.268
But there's a very big difference
between us.

28:08.436 --> 28:11.147
You keep turning your back on your past.

28:12.065 --> 28:13.441
But I will face my past.

28:14.234 --> 28:16.820
And it will ensure that I survive.

28:17.320 --> 28:20.448
[laughs]

28:26.579 --> 28:30.166
[breathing deeply]

28:30.250 --> 28:32.252
[foreboding music]

28:38.800 --> 28:40.969
[upbeat music playing]

28:48.852 --> 28:51.146
[both grunting]

28:56.234 --> 28:59.154
[Kuina breathing heavily]

29:03.324 --> 29:05.827
[sword clanging]

29:10.331 --> 29:11.458
[grunts]

29:11.541 --> 29:14.294
[intense music]

29:17.088 --> 29:18.506
[groans]

29:21.009 --> 29:22.510
[groaning continues]

29:26.973 --> 29:28.433
[grunts]

29:29.017 --> 29:30.435
[glass shatters]

29:30.518 --> 29:33.188
[fire alarm ringing]

29:50.955 --> 29:53.416
[soft piano music]

29:54.709 --> 29:57.545
[Chota]
Do you remember that arcade that closed?

29:57.629 --> 29:58.797
What was its name again?

29:58.880 --> 30:01.257
Uh, it was
in front of our high school, right?

30:01.341 --> 30:03.343
- [Karube] What the hell was it again?
- Dream World.

30:04.093 --> 30:06.012
- You're right, Dream World!
- [laughter]

30:06.095 --> 30:08.348
That's it! It was Dream World.

30:10.767 --> 30:13.853
I'd skip class to go there
and Arisu would already be there.

30:13.937 --> 30:16.439
Eyes glued to some dirty magazine,
reading it out loud.

30:17.190 --> 30:19.400
The porn magazines in the '90s were
the best.

30:19.484 --> 30:21.903
Yeah, they were really good.

30:22.487 --> 30:25.990
Actually, I liked reading the articles.
They were well-written.

30:27.534 --> 30:31.579
The day the arcade went bankrupt,
Arisu stood in front of the building

30:31.663 --> 30:33.665
- and cried.
- Yep, just me and the owner.

30:33.748 --> 30:35.333
[laughter]

30:36.584 --> 30:39.712
Ah, those days were the best.

30:39.796 --> 30:42.799
Even though we bitched about it,
high school was awesome.

30:43.383 --> 30:44.425
[Karube sighs]

30:46.302 --> 30:47.262
[Karube] Arisu.

30:49.889 --> 30:51.724
Do something with your life.

30:53.518 --> 30:55.812
Yeah. And remember us.

30:55.895 --> 30:57.230
Promise, Arisu?

30:57.313 --> 30:59.524
[sentimental music]

31:15.123 --> 31:18.960
[muffled cough]

31:24.090 --> 31:26.092
[coughing continues]

31:33.308 --> 31:36.185
[grunting]

31:42.817 --> 31:46.362
[grunting continues]

31:56.623 --> 31:57.957
[retches]

32:02.170 --> 32:04.881
[coughing]

32:06.341 --> 32:09.177
[breathing heavily]

32:17.477 --> 32:20.563
[coughing]

32:21.481 --> 32:22.607
[weakly]
Help me.

32:24.275 --> 32:25.360
I'm here.

32:27.153 --> 32:28.196
Someone!

32:29.197 --> 32:31.407
- [fire alarm ringing]
- [all panting]

32:31.491 --> 32:32.450
Smoke?

32:33.826 --> 32:36.245
- [Tatta] Huh? Is there a fire?
- [Usagi shushes]

32:38.122 --> 32:39.332
I hear someone.

32:47.340 --> 32:51.219
[Arisu shouting faintly]
Help! Someone!

32:51.302 --> 32:52.261
[exclaims]

33:08.361 --> 33:09.821
[Arisu shouts faintly]
Someone, help me!

33:10.905 --> 33:12.323
In here!

33:12.407 --> 33:14.117
- Arisu!
- [door rattles]

33:14.200 --> 33:15.827
The door won't open!

33:17.662 --> 33:19.747
[gunshots]

33:20.456 --> 33:23.084
- [man grunts]
- [panting]

33:27.797 --> 33:29.048
- [gunshot]
- [Usagi yelps]

33:31.134 --> 33:32.844
- [Tatta screams]
- [gunshot]

33:38.141 --> 33:40.184
- [yells]
- [thuds]

33:40.268 --> 33:41.978
[gasps]

33:43.187 --> 33:45.523
- I did that.
- [Asahi] I can't do this anymore.

33:46.482 --> 33:48.901
- [shrieks]
- [grunts]

33:50.361 --> 33:52.196
[gasps]

33:55.992 --> 33:58.536
[window shattering]

34:00.955 --> 34:02.165
Arisu!

34:03.791 --> 34:04.709
Usagi.

34:10.715 --> 34:12.967
[upbeat techno music playing]

34:13.051 --> 34:14.510
- [Kuina grunts]
- [glass shatters]

34:19.640 --> 34:20.808
[laughs]

34:23.144 --> 34:26.939
[cackling]

34:27.023 --> 34:28.483
- [glass shatters]
- [grunts]

34:43.206 --> 34:46.042
Is that all you've got? Hmm?

34:48.461 --> 34:50.129
I knew it when I saw you.

34:51.798 --> 34:54.258
Your will to survive is weak.

34:56.385 --> 34:57.720
It's weak, is it?

34:58.888 --> 34:59.889
Really?

35:24.372 --> 35:25.414
Hikari?

35:40.847 --> 35:43.516
You look completely different.

35:51.023 --> 35:52.275
To me…

35:54.485 --> 35:57.405
you look beautiful.

35:59.031 --> 36:01.033
[soft music]

36:04.245 --> 36:05.288
[laughs softly]

36:17.592 --> 36:20.011
[Kuina's mother cries]

36:22.597 --> 36:23.598
Thank you.

36:25.266 --> 36:27.643
[emotional music]

36:31.189 --> 36:33.441
[glasses crackling]

36:34.984 --> 36:37.486
[exhales deeply]

36:59.675 --> 37:01.677
[techno music playing]

37:01.761 --> 37:04.305
[yells]

37:04.889 --> 37:06.265
[grunts]

37:06.349 --> 37:07.475
[groans]

37:07.558 --> 37:11.062
[shouting in slow motion]

37:11.145 --> 37:12.772
[Last Boss screams]

37:19.737 --> 37:21.280
- [shouts]
- [Last Boss yelps]

37:23.950 --> 37:26.160
[panting]

37:29.497 --> 37:31.332
"Never hesitate to strike."

37:32.833 --> 37:34.418
I have done as you taught me,

37:35.169 --> 37:36.254
Father.

37:39.465 --> 37:41.259
[both panting]

37:49.392 --> 37:50.559
It's good to see you.

37:51.352 --> 37:53.396
- You're okay?
- Uh-huh, thank you.

37:55.856 --> 37:59.068
I hate to break this to you now,
but we only have 30 minutes left.

38:00.861 --> 38:03.489
Okay, explain the rules to me quickly.
[panting]

38:04.115 --> 38:06.033
[gunshots]

38:08.869 --> 38:10.162
[gun cocks]

38:11.872 --> 38:12.999
Out of ammo.

38:15.167 --> 38:19.046
[Tetsuya] We've killed a lot of them,
but we still haven't found the witch.

38:20.840 --> 38:23.759
- [gunshots in distance]
- [screaming in distance]

38:23.843 --> 38:25.553
What the hell are we doing?

38:27.888 --> 38:30.266
This is the worst of the games yet.

38:31.183 --> 38:34.437
But just like those horse-headed taggers
we met before,

38:34.520 --> 38:38.274
they were forced to participate
with rules of their own.

38:39.025 --> 38:40.943
I'm sure it's the…
[pants]

38:41.027 --> 38:42.862
…the same this time.

38:42.945 --> 38:45.614
The witch had to kill that girl
to start the game

38:45.698 --> 38:47.950
and try to survive until the end of it.

38:48.034 --> 38:49.952
In other words, the witch clears the game

38:50.036 --> 38:51.704
if everyone at the Beach gets a Game Over,

38:51.787 --> 38:52.955
or gets killed by the laser.

38:53.539 --> 38:55.833
But who the hell could be the witch?

38:55.916 --> 38:57.668
If I were the witch,

38:58.461 --> 39:00.087
I'd join the others in the hunt.

39:00.713 --> 39:02.715
Because it'd be Game Over if I was caught.

39:03.841 --> 39:06.594
So, it's someone in the militant corps?

39:06.677 --> 39:09.430
Niragi, Last Boss, or Aguni, huh?

39:09.513 --> 39:11.390
No. If that was the case,

39:11.474 --> 39:13.726
the militant corps would simply kill
each other.

39:13.809 --> 39:16.812
It doesn't feel like
that's the purpose of the game.

39:17.396 --> 39:18.939
The purpose of the game?

39:19.023 --> 39:20.816
This is a Hearts game.

39:20.900 --> 39:22.068
[breathing heavily]

39:22.151 --> 39:23.903
It's not just a physical game.

39:24.487 --> 39:27.323
I know because I've cleared
a Hearts game before.

39:27.406 --> 39:29.784
It's the most evil of the games.

39:29.867 --> 39:31.744
You toy with people's feelings.

39:32.328 --> 39:35.915
You betray and try to kill each other.

39:36.540 --> 39:39.877
The Hearts game can eat away at your soul.

39:41.420 --> 39:45.633
Even if the militant corps wins,
other conflicts will turn up.

39:46.509 --> 39:48.803
[Tatta] So, what should we do?

39:51.889 --> 39:53.474
Something's not right.

39:55.309 --> 39:56.644
What could it be?

39:57.228 --> 39:59.230
[eerie music]

40:00.606 --> 40:02.191
[Arisu] If I was the witch,

40:03.067 --> 40:04.777
how would I steer…

40:04.860 --> 40:06.487
the game to win?

40:08.489 --> 40:10.950
[fire crackling]

40:24.046 --> 40:26.048
[eerie music continues]

40:31.345 --> 40:32.596
[thuds]

40:55.369 --> 40:56.871
[Hatter] It doesn't suit you.

40:56.954 --> 40:58.289
[chuckles]

41:01.125 --> 41:03.544
Who would've thought
that the best men's club host in Kabukicho

41:03.627 --> 41:04.795
would wind up being a hatter?

41:04.879 --> 41:06.046
[rustles]

41:06.130 --> 41:09.383
It was my father's dying wish.
[sniffs]

41:10.176 --> 41:12.553
You were an SDF officer, weren't you?

41:14.221 --> 41:16.807
You could've done anything
but join the yakuza.

41:19.477 --> 41:20.644
Speaking of the yakuza,

41:21.437 --> 41:24.482
Shogo was killed
for skimming the government's payoff.

41:25.483 --> 41:27.276
[indistinct chattering]

41:31.614 --> 41:34.992
You know, you're the only old friend
that I've still got left.

41:36.410 --> 41:37.703
Live long, friend.

41:40.289 --> 41:41.415
You too.

41:45.336 --> 41:47.421
[fire crackling]

42:04.271 --> 42:05.272
No.

42:07.149 --> 42:11.028
[Arisu] I shouldn't be putting myself
in the witch's shoes.

42:11.737 --> 42:14.281
I should be in the shoes
of the game master.

42:15.282 --> 42:16.325
Game master?

42:17.076 --> 42:17.993
Don't you see?

42:18.077 --> 42:21.830
The game was designed to suit
both its location and its players.

42:22.665 --> 42:24.291
Right after Hatter was killed,

42:24.375 --> 42:25.876
Momoka was murdered.

42:26.460 --> 42:28.671
Someone who knows
the ins and outs of the Beach…

42:28.754 --> 42:30.881
constructed the game and its timing.

42:31.715 --> 42:33.634
They constructed the timing?

42:33.717 --> 42:36.762
The two deaths didn't happen
at the same time by chance.

42:38.639 --> 42:42.726
It's like that that the game master
has been waiting for this moment.

42:43.227 --> 42:44.645
Seriously?

42:45.813 --> 42:47.773
Then, who's the witch?

42:49.441 --> 42:53.946
Hatter's death was announced
after Momoka died.

42:54.863 --> 42:57.199
The only people who knew
of his death before that…

42:57.783 --> 43:00.452
were the militant corps
and the executives.

43:00.536 --> 43:06.792
But the game master may have known
about Hatter's death too.

43:07.418 --> 43:11.714
Then everyone at the Beach is a suspect.

43:11.797 --> 43:15.259
When I passed by the lobby
an hour before the game started,

43:15.884 --> 43:18.095
Momoka's body wasn't there.

43:19.805 --> 43:22.057
Someone must have moved her body there

43:22.141 --> 43:23.892
sometime during that hour.

43:23.976 --> 43:26.854
No point questioning someone.
The witch can simply lie.

43:26.937 --> 43:28.063
The question is…

43:30.608 --> 43:33.402
why did the game start when it did?

43:34.987 --> 43:37.072
Why did they wait for Hatter's death

43:37.656 --> 43:39.325
before starting the game?

43:40.784 --> 43:41.952
I'm guessing it was…

43:42.911 --> 43:45.372
to throw the Beach
into a state of confusion.

43:45.456 --> 43:46.665
If that's true…

43:48.083 --> 43:50.836
[Arisu] If I were the game master,
what would I do next?

43:54.089 --> 43:56.175
[water burbling]

43:58.844 --> 44:00.846
[slow suspenseful music]

44:15.736 --> 44:17.029
But of course.

44:19.198 --> 44:20.240
I know who it is!

44:24.203 --> 44:25.663
- [thwacks]
- [grunts]

44:27.915 --> 44:30.501
If we stop here,
then all we did would be pointless.

44:30.584 --> 44:31.877
We can't stop now!

44:31.960 --> 44:33.962
[suspenseful music]

44:41.637 --> 44:44.515
[announcer] Time remaining, 20 minutes.

44:54.692 --> 44:56.777
[music fades]

44:58.570 --> 44:59.696
What is it?

45:03.951 --> 45:05.285
I think that I know…

45:07.579 --> 45:08.872
who the witch is.

45:08.956 --> 45:11.333
[suspenseful music intensifies]

45:14.336 --> 45:16.338
[closing theme music]
